  II. THE CONSONANCE HIERARCHY OF GAPS
  ----------------------------------------

  Gaps with correction = 1 (no boost): g has no odd prime factors.
  These are g = powers of 2: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, ...
  Gaps 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64: all have the BASELINE twin prime density.
  They are the 'unison' gaps — no harmonic coloring.

  Gaps with correction = 2 (octave boost): 3 | g but 5,7 don't.
  g = 3, 6, 12, 24, 48: all get an octave of extra density.
  They are TWICE as common as twin primes (per unit).

  Gaps with correction = 4/3 (fourth boost): 5 | g but 3,7 don't.
  g = 5, 10, 20, 25, 40: get a fourth of extra density.
  33% more common than twins.


